INT8 GEMM fragment loads and reduction traversal from MLX

Upstream revision: 25532871329fe4cafdada9fa0941a1cdbfb3a9f2
Repository: https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx
License: MIT (included in gemm.metal.inc).

gemm.metal.inc embeds utils.h, steel/gemm/gemm_nax.h and
steel/gemm/kernels/steel_gemm_fused_nax.h with their transitive local includes.
Duplicate includes and pragma-once directives were removed and the result
wrapped in a C++ raw string. Unused GEMM entry points were omitted. Upstream copyright notices are retained.

NAInt8MatMulKernel uses the integer fragment implementation with its existing
activation quantizer and row scales. Its local generator unrolls pairs of K32
operations and removes masked loads for complete K32 fragments inside a K512
tail. The final partial fragment retains bounds checks. INT32 accumulation,
FP16 row scales, bias and output match the existing INT8 operator.

Implementation choice is a kernel-source property; alignment is specialized
at pipeline creation. Matrix dimensions and grid sizes are supplied at encode
time. No FP16 GEMM or attention operator is instantiated from this source.
